(6006999, 877926, 13688, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smardaz:</b></div><hr/><i> all critique can be helpful, i notice you only marked the compliment as helpful.....You can''t be surprised that the voters saw a shot of a guitar and didn''t think of team sports? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Unfortunately, only one of the comments actually had to do with the technicals of the photo.  This will always be the problem with the site in that it focuses too much on parameters.  Based on your details I can see why only 1 comment was useful.  For me, compositionally the guitar strap connector is kind of annoying.  I like the gritty nature of the photo, it feels road weary, but  I think it might have been more interesting if you tried to incorporate more of the environment to help solidify the tour concept or the returning home concept.  And sports being pastimes and a band being a team isn''t really that much of a stretch for someone with an ounce of creativity to make, so it is even more ridiculous that people would feel the need to focus on what this photo isn''t about.  Unfortunately that is the governing mindset here.  How''d the tour go?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-05-14 10:23:09.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by smardaz: all critique can be helpful, i notice you only marked the compliment as helpful.....You can''t be surprised that the voters saw a shot of a guitar and didn''t think of team sports?  Unfortunately, only one of the comments actually had to do with the technicals of the photo.  This will always be the problem with the site in that it focuses too much on parameters.  Based on your details I can see why only 1 comment was useful.  For me, compositionally the guitar strap connector is kind of annoying.  I like the gritty nature of the photo, it feels road weary, but  I think it might have been more interesting if you tried to incorporate more of the environment to help solidify the tour concept or the returning home concept.  And sports being pastimes and a band being a team isn''t really that much of a stretch for someone with an ounce of creativity to make, so it is even more ridiculous that people would feel the need to focus on what this photo isn''t about.  Unfortunately that is the governing mindset here.  How''d the tour go?', '2010-05-14 11:22:15.000000', '2010-05-14 11:23:09.000000', 0),
(6007585, 877926, 114472, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by muur88:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Unfortunately, only one of the comments actually had to do with the technicals of the photo.  This will always be the problem with the site in that it focuses too much on parameters.  Based on your details I can see why only 1 comment was useful.  For me, compositionally the guitar strap connector is kind of annoying.  I like the gritty nature of the photo, it feels road weary, but  I think it might have been more interesting if you tried to incorporate more of the environment to help solidify the tour concept or the returning home concept.  And sports being pastimes and a band being a team isn''t really that much of a stretch for someone with an ounce of creativity to make, so it is even more ridiculous that people would feel the need to focus on what this photo isn''t about.  Unfortunately that is the governing mindset here.  How''d the tour go? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree with you. The fact that I only found 1 comment to be useful indeed has to do with the technical aspect of it. Comments don''t need to be all positive to be ranked useful by me, but I can''t do anything with a comment about why this is not sports. I thought maybe people could see beyond the typical idea of sports, but I guess not :). No problem, I''ve probably weren''t supposed to think people would see the picture the same as I do. Anyway, I do appreciate your thoughts about the picture and the ways this could have been improved. Always good help for following challenges.<br/> <br/>The tour was truly awesome! Thnx for asking. It is definitely something I could do all the time. Who knows, maybe some day :).<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-05-14 18:00:52.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by muur88: Unfortunately, only one of the comments actually had to do with the technicals of the photo.  This will always be the problem with the site in that it focuses too much on parameters.  Based on your details I can see why only 1 comment was useful.  For me, compositionally the guitar strap connector is kind of annoying.  I like the gritty nature of the photo, it feels road weary, but  I think it might have been more interesting if you tried to incorporate more of the environment to help solidify the tour concept or the returning home concept.  And sports being pastimes and a band being a team isn''t really that much of a stretch for someone with an ounce of creativity to make, so it is even more ridiculous that people would feel the need to focus on what this photo isn''t about.  Unfortunately that is the governing mindset here.  How''d the tour go?   I agree with you. The fact that I only found 1 comment to be useful indeed has to do with the technical aspect of it. Comments don''t need to be all positive to be ranked useful by me, but I can''t do anything with a comment about why this is not sports. I thought maybe people could see beyond the typical idea of sports, but I guess not :). No problem, I''ve probably weren''t supposed to think people would see the picture the same as I do. Anyway, I do appreciate your thoughts about the picture and the ways this could have been improved. Always good help for following challenges. The tour was truly awesome! Thnx for asking. It is definitely something I could do all the time. Who knows, maybe some day :).', '2010-05-14 18:59:12.000000', '2010-05-14 19:00:52.000000', 0),
(6007790, 878179, 75034, '<td valign="top">Scott, great work on this shot. It was my pick to win and I''m glad it did. I think you did everything right with your image. I love the subject, concept, the composition, colour, editing........ everything!<br/> <br/>Good on you and a blue after only eight challenges. I can''t wait to see what other images your going to offer up to us here at DPC.<br/> <br/>Thank you for sharing your talents with us. Keep them coming.<br/> <br/>MAX!</td>', 'Scott, great work on this shot. It was my pick to win and I''m glad it did. I think you did everything right with your image. I love the subject, concept, the composition, colour, editing........ everything! Good on you and a blue after only eight challenges. I can''t wait to see what other images your going to offer up to us here at DPC. Thank you for sharing your talents with us. Keep them coming. MAX!', '2010-05-14 23:34:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6007798, 878288, 75034, '<td valign="top">Gediminas, Great lighting and capture with this entry. I love the splash of dirt over the ball and the positioning of the ball in your shot. Very well thought out and executed great editing and tack sharp.<br/> <br/>You and Scott (First place) both beat me to a ribbon, him in 7 you in 23. It took me 104 to do it.<br/> <br/>Looking forward to seeing what else your going to bring to us.<br/> <br/>All the best to you and yours.<br/> <br/>MAX!</td>', 'Gediminas, Great lighting and capture with this entry. I love the splash of dirt over the ball and the positioning of the ball in your shot. Very well thought out and executed great editing and tack sharp. You and Scott (First place) both beat me to a ribbon, him in 7 you in 23. It took me 104 to do it. Looking forward to seeing what else your going to bring to us. All the best to you and yours. MAX!', '2010-05-14 23:47:05.000000', NULL, 0),
